UNIT-3 Pig

We created a sample file named:
simple_logs.txt

google.com    10    100    2026-01-01
youtube.com   10    150    2026-01-01
google.com    11    200    2026-01-01
facebook.com  11     50    2026-01-01
google.com    10    120    2026-01-02
youtube.com   10     80    2026-01-02
The fields in the actual file were separated by tab characters.

Step 1 — Create the HDFS directory
At the Linux terminal, we ran:
	hdfs dfs -mkdir -p data/pig/simple_logs

	hdfs dfs -put simple_logs.txt data/pig/simple_logs/

	hdfs dfs -ls data/pig/simple_logs/

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 2 — Create a Pig script
nano hour_day.pig

logs = LOAD 'data/pig/simple_logs'
USING PigStorage('\t')
AS (
    site:chararray,
    hour_of_day:int,
    page_views:int,
    data_date:chararray
);

grouped_logs = GROUP logs BY (hour_of_day, data_date);

total_views = FOREACH grouped_logs GENERATE
    group.hour_of_day AS hour,
    group.data_date AS date,
    SUM(logs.page_views) AS total_page_views;

DUMP total_views;

